    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.contract_nodes_multi - EdgeCase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.contract_nodes_multi.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.contract_nodes_multi()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Contract multiple nodes into a single node.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.contract_nodes_multi()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Contract multiple nodes into a single node.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.contract_nodes_multi()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Contract multiple nodes into a single node.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nContract multiple nodes into a single node.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L48996-L49132){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.contract_nodes_multi(\n    nodes,\n    self_loops=True,\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Contract several nodes](../assets/graphs/contract-nodes-multi.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"Before: a six-node graph in two rows with B, E, and F grouped in a tinted region; B, first in the list, is outlined as the survivor and E and F are in the accent color. After: E and F are gone, shown dashed. Their outside edge from D now attaches to B, and the edges inside the group collapse into one self-loop on B.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nMerges all specified nodes into the first node in the list. All edges incident to any of the\ncontracted nodes are redirected to the first node. Edges between contracted nodes become\nself-loops (if `self_loops=True`).\n\nThis generalizes `contract_nodes()` and `contracted_edge()` to a whole group at once, and\nthe nodes do not need to be adjacent. Use it to collapse a set of nodes that should be\ntreated as one unit, for example:\n\n- summarizing a detected community, department, or region as a single node while keeping\n  its links to the rest of the network\n- merging duplicate records of the same entity (entity resolution)\n- simplifying a dense cluster before layout or further analysis\n\nEdges at the merged node that end up connecting the same pair of nodes are collapsed into\none (the first one found keeps its weight and attributes), and all edges inside the group\ncollapse into at most one self-loop. Edges between other nodes, parallel ones included,\nare kept as they are. The remaining nodes keep their IDs, labels and\nattributes, and surviving edges keep their IDs. The original graph is not modified. To\ncollapse *every* group of a partition in one step, use `quotient_graph()`.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[nodes]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [list[int | str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   List of node IDs or labels to contract. The first node is the target; all other nodes\n    are merged into it, so it keeps its ID and label. Entries should be unique: repeating\n    the first node raises a `ValueError` and repeating another node raises a `KeyError`.\n    A single-element list returns an unchanged copy.\n\n<code>[self_loops]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[True]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   If `True` (default), edges between contracted nodes become self-loops. If `False`, such\n    edges are removed. Use `False` when the internal connections of the group are not of\n    interest or when later algorithms do not handle self-loops.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Graph]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   A new graph with all specified nodes contracted into one. It has `len(nodes) - 1`\n    fewer nodes than the original.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [KeyError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If any node ID does not exist.\n\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If the node list is empty, if a label is not found, or if the first node appears again\n    later in the list.\n:::\n\n## Technical Notes {.doc-technical-notes}\n\nRepeated contraction costs $O(k \\cdot E)$ for $k$ nodes: each merge scans the\ncurrent edge list, and after each merge the graph is one node smaller. The head of\nthe list is the surviving node, inheriting every edge that touched any member of\nthe batch; the remaining nodes disappear along with their labels and attributes, while\nthe survivor keeps its own. This is the natural\nbuilding block for community-quotienting workflows where an entire cluster collapses\nto a single representative before further analysis.\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~contract_nodes`) \n\n:   Merge just two nodes.\n\n[](`~quotient_graph`) \n\n:   Collapse every block of a partition at once.\n\n[](`~cmty_louvain`) \n\n:   Find communities to collapse.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nA triangle \"A\", \"B\", \"C\" with a tail to \"D\" collapses into a single node \"A\". The three\ntriangle edges become one self-loop, and the link to \"D\" is kept:\n\n::: {#84aa390b .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ng = ec.Graph.from_edges([(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"B\", \"C\"), (\"C\", \"A\"), (\"C\", \"D\")])\n\nmerged = g.contract_nodes_multi([\"A\", \"B\", \"C\"])\nmerged.get_edges_str_repr(use_labels=True)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n['A--A', 'A--D']\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nWith `self_loops=False`, the group's internal edges are discarded:\n\n::: {#abc5cdd6 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nmerged = g.contract_nodes_multi([\"A\", \"B\", \"C\"], self_loops=False)\nmerged.get_edges_str_repr(use_labels=True)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n['A--D']\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### One community as one node\n\nLouvain finds four communities in the karate club. Collapsing the administrator's\ncommunity into a single node keeps every other member as they were, and shows how that\ncommunity connects to the rest of the club:\n\n::: {#942cdbdc .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nkarate = ec.karate_club()\nmembership = karate.cmty_louvain(return_dict=True)\nkarate.set_node_attrs(\"community\", membership)\n\nhome = membership[karate.get_id_from_label(\"33\")]\ncommunity = [node for node, c in membership.items() if c == home]\n\nclub = karate.contract_nodes_multi(community, self_loops=False)\nlen(community), club.count_nodes()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```\n(11, 24)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nThe 11 members become one node, which takes the label of the lowest-numbered member, 8.\nIt's tied to 10 members outside the community:\n\n::: {#80fd9eed .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nmerged = sorted(community)[0]\n\nclub.get_label_from_id(merged), club.get_degree(merged)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}\n```\n('8', 10)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nColored by the original communities, the merged node is the only one left of its\ncommunity, and sits between the instructor's community and the six members of the fourth:\n\n::: {#8e9551e5 .cell execution_count=5}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nclub.plot(color_by=\"community\", label_by=\"label\", seed=2)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=5}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}</style><div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"position:relative;width:fit-content;max-width:100%;margin:1em auto\">\n<style>.ec-plot > svg { display:block; max-width:100%; height:auto; }</style>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org